  {
   "id": 41,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Rates and what is not here yet",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 62,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 7
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "**Rates (from the owner's AES Ohio bills, 2026-04-28 to 2026-09-22; derived by Claude, not billed per-kWh figures [UNVERIFIED]):**\n- The default rate is the **marginal** $0.2094/kWh: supply $23.13 + \"other delivery charges\" $21.48 over 213.08 kWh on the latest bill, leaving out the fixed $9.75 customer charge. It assumes \"other delivery charges\" scale with kWh. The **all-in average** ($54.36 / 213.08 kWh) is $0.2551/kWh. Pick either in the `rate` list at the top. A straight-line fit over five bills gives about $8.23 + $0.2053/kWh. Update the list when a new bill arrives.\n\n**Plugs:** both plugs report watts, volts, amps and energy (server `192.168.1.66`, PC `192.168.1.6`). The cost charts accumulate only from when each plug was installed, and a projection from a short history is rough: the PC's draw changes a lot with harness load and gaming.\n\n**Not here yet:** the PC's GPU load, replay-archive size and Loki logs. Big-number view for the screen: dashboard \"Hiveplex at a glance (kiosk)\"."
   }
  }
